NNOOTTEESS
       Once a thread has been detached, it can’t be joined with
       pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn(3) or be made joinable again.

       A new thread can be created in a detached state using
       pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__sseettddeettaacchhssttaattee(3) to set the detached attribute of the
       _a_t_t_r argument of pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3).

       The detached attribute merely determines the behavior of the system
       when the thread terminates; it does not prevent the thread from being
       terminated if the process terminates using eexxiitt(3) (or equivalently, if
       the main thread returns).

       Either pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn(3) or pptthhrreeaadd__ddeettaacchh() should be called for each
       thread that an application creates, so that system resources for the
       thread can be released.  (But note that the resources of any threads
       for which one of these actions has not been done will be freed when the
       process terminates.)

